  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models with avgpool are promising, especially config_005 with scvi_n200 at 0.650 accuracy and 0.628 F1, while image-only and transformer-aggregation variants are weaker. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the current best performance is specific to scvi_n200 or whether another RNA representation, scgpt, can improve further under the same multiprofile avgpool setting. config_008 tests this by changing only the RNA encoder relative to the current best RNA configuration, isolating the effect of representation. It is the best next experiment because it either identifies a stronger encoder or confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred representation before adding more complexity such as fusion."
